ourse_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{3}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c8d5431f2416a11a2ffd140598219391744997246558f294f0abd839312a40a" "basis" 1467 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/state.json" "file_sha256" "5c8d5431f2416a11a2ffd140598219391744997246558f294f0abd839312a40a" "basis" 1467 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040753/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-39435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $‖3u+v‖=18$ and $‖u‖=5$, find the smallest possible value of $‖v‖.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the triangle inequality, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3u+v‖ & \\le 3‖u‖+‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3u+v‖ & \\le 3‖u‖+‖v‖ \\\\ 18 & \\le 3\\cdot 5+‖v‖ \\\\ 18 & \\le 15+‖v‖ \\\\ 3 & \\le ‖v‖.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the smallest possible value of $‖v‖$ is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39435" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcc2292f59387dedcb16ca29b8c9b08985fc0b000c2a861976443666f533d5c5"} {"question" "q-39435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "\\frac{18}{13}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39435" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2}=50$ and $‖u‖=‖w‖=4$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & =|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =16‖v{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\  & =17‖v{‖}^{2}+16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}50 & \\le 17‖v‖+16 \\\\ 34 & \\le 17‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $2\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $\\sqrt{2}\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcc2292f59387dedcb16ca29b8c9b08985fc0b000c2a861976443666f533d5c5"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-39610" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-74189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2}=101$ and $‖u‖=‖w‖=2$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-74189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}101 & ={|u\\cdot v|}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =4‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4‖v{‖}^{2}+5‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =4‖v{‖}^{2}+5(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & =4‖v{‖}^{2}+5(‖v{‖}^{2}+{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}101 & \\le 9‖v‖+20 \\\\ 81 & \\le 9‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 9 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $9\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $3\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-74189" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcc2292f59387dedcb16ca29b8c9b08985fc0b000c2a861976443666f533d5c5"} {"question" "q-74189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-74189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "\\sqrt{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-74189" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let the vectors $v$ and $w$ be orthogonal. \nIf $|u\\cdot v{|}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2}=62$ and $‖u‖=‖w‖=3$, then what is the minimum possible value of $‖v‖?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, using the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}62 & ={|u\\cdot v|}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {‖u{‖}^{2}\\cdot ‖v‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}\\cdot ‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $v⊥w$, using the Pythagorean theorem, simplifying, and substituting in the given information, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9‖v{‖}^{2}+4‖v+w{‖}^{2} & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4(‖v{‖}^{2}+‖w{‖}^{2}) \\\\  & =9‖v{‖}^{2}+4(‖v{‖}^{2}+{3}^{2}) \\\\  & =13‖v{‖}^{2}+36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCombining the two steps above, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}62 & \\le 13‖v{‖}^{2}+36 \\\\ 26 & \\le 13‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 2 & \\le ‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $2\\le ‖v{‖}^{2}$ implies that $\\sqrt{2}\\le ‖v‖.$ Notice that we disregard the negative solutions since the norm can't be negative.\n\nTherefore, the minimum possible value of $‖v‖$ is $\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/state.json" "file_sha256" "5f2b2f027dcd27300c5912f0f21a1a9c0e952681f276eb178e3b339327256336"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068385/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "dcc2292f59387dedcb16ca29b8c9b08985fc0b000c2a861976443666f533d5c5"} {"question" "q-74191" "field" "selection" "a